    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0391" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7922½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-25T11:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 25, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3.11 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I find the French Prime Minister a firm believer in unity of military direction
                    but doubtful of the plan suggested by his predecessor and the British Prime
                    Minister which resulted in the formation of the Supreme War Council. I believe
                    something more practical <pb facs="0392" n="318" xml:id="pg318"/> must be worked
                    out and [this] Bliss and I are trying to do. The French Prime Minister assures
                    me that he will cordially cooperate. The French Chief of Staff and the Prime
                    Minister will confer with Bliss and me this afternoon upon the subject.</p>
                <p>I am refusing to be drawn into any of their controversies, particularly those
                    concerning war aims of a territorial nature. We must, I think, hold to the broad
                    principles you have laid down and not get mixed in the small and selfish
                    ones.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
